summary:
I wrote $HOME/projects/llm/docs/opencode.md. That is the only file I created or changed. I wrote it with the Write tool, then made two small edits with a Python string replace.

The doc covers:
- the OpenCode v2.3.0 config shape, as a key table with links to the docs and the v2.3.0 source;
- the validated two-provider config, as a JSON block;
- matching rules: modelID must equal --served-model-name or --alias, and limit.context must equal --max-model-len or -c, with a table of which server settings each entry assumes;
- why built-in vLLM discovery turns tools off, and the two ways around it;
- thinking variants and reasoning fields for each runtime, and why thinking stays off by default (the DGX numbers are labeled as measured on the DGX Spark, not this laptop);
- the context budget: a 64k floor, 5.5k to 7k tokens of fixed prompt marked as an estimate, and the compaction arithmetic;
- Ollama notes, with a validated snippet;
- the four OpenCode issues, re-checked live on 2026-11-15: all open, fix PRs #60219 and #58053 unmerged, llama.cpp PR #26939 merged on 2026-08-20;
- trying models on OpenRouter first: which picks are hosted and their model ids, that hosted quality is an upper bound for local quants, and the privacy settings. These include the review check's corrections on Safety Retention and the "ZDR only" setting, and on Qwen3.8's 1,024,000 listed context.

Changes to the config in opencode-proposed.json: following the audit fix, I added a qwen3.8-27b entry on llama.cpp. It uses modelID "local", 65536 context, and capabilities.reasoning.effort set to none, low and medium. I did not add an agents.title or agents.compaction pin, also per the audit. I re-validated with python3 -I and jsonschema 4.19.2 (Draft 2020-12) against scratchpad/opencode-schema.json, which is identical to oc/schema.json. All three JSON blocks in the doc have 0 errors, and a negative test with a V1 npm key fails as it should.

New fact verified from the v2.3.0 source clone and the cached OpenCode docs: OpenCode's native OpenRouter provider reads OPENROUTER_API_KEY. Non-connection keys in settings, such as settings.provider with data_collection, zdr and require_parameters, are passed into the request body (settings.ts toConfig, openrouter.ts bodyOptions).

Checks on the file: it contains no em or en dash and no non-ASCII characters. Every cited URL returned HTTP 200 on 2026-11-15.
